; Entity handler: the spawner of the crusaders (kind 1, rooms 5, 6 and 25)
;
; An invisible object that makes a new crusader from a template every 40 passes of the main loop (one pass per frame in
; the chase rooms): the slot counts down the animation
; counter at +$12 (the first count, 90 passes, is the parameter byte 1 of the room object record: the first crusader
; appears 90 passes after the room is entered; the reload at +$13 is not used afterwards, a constant 40 is loaded
; instead). When the counter reaches 0 it asks #R$8A70 for a free slot and goes on at #R$B0B1, which copies the
; template into it. The template (#R$B04C) is pointed to by the slot word +4, from the parameter bytes 5 and 6 of the
; record (#R$8BBB, #R$8BC6, #R$8BD1); each room has its own path script. The slot never changes: crusaders keep coming
; for as long as Jean stays in the room (observed in room 5: four or five on the screen at a time, a new one every
; 40 passes).
; .
; Slot fields used: +4 word template address; +$12 byte counter, +$13 byte reload (not used). Its x, y and sprite fields
; are not used (nothing is drawn).
; .
; Hardware: none.
;
; SP Slot address + 2
@label=UpdateCrusaderSpawner
c$B099 POP DE        ; skip +2 (speed, 0)
 $B09A POP DE        ; DE = +4: the template of the crusaders
 $B09B LD HL,$000C   ; skip +6..+$11: the position and sprite fields, six words
 $B09E ADD HL,SP     ;
 $B09F LD SP,HL      ; SP = slot + $12
 $B0A0 POP BC        ; C = counter, B = reload
 $B0A1 DEC C         ;
 $B0A2 JR NZ,$B0A6   ;
@isub=LD C,CRUSADER_PERIOD
 $B0A4 LD C,$28      ; every 40 passes from now on
*$B0A6 PUSH BC       ; store the counter (SP back at slot + $12)
 $B0A7 JP NZ,$B41F   ; NextSlotAfterAnim: not yet
 $B0AA LD IY,$B0B1   ; the free slot search returns to #R$B0B1
@isub=JP FindFreeSlot_IY
 $B0AE JP $8A70      ; find a free slot: IX = slot, carry set when there is one
